RETAIL TRADE
Retail trade refers to sale of goods in small lots to the final consumers. A retailer
buys goods from a wholesaler and sells them to the consumer. So, he acts as a link
between the wholesaler and the ultimate consumer.
Features of Retail Trade
Retailer is the last link in the distribution chain.
Retailer sells the goods or services directly to consumers.
Retailer deals with a variety of products.
Retailer buys and sells a small quantity of goods.
Retailer is generally located in residential areas.
Retailer maintains personal relations with the customers.
• Retailer may contact the customers on telephone, Internet, TV or
through his retail showroom.
Retailer acts as a middleman between wholesalers and customers.
